   "title": "Read me",
   "properties": {},
   "widgets_values": [
    "## Grading during sampling\n\nThe wheels on the **latent** node change the model's own prediction at every step, so the picture is *composed* in the graded look instead of having it laid over the top. Shadows get the colour you asked for because the model put it there, not because a filter pushed it.\n\nNo input image is needed — this generates from the prompt, so it runs straight away.\n\nThe lower sampler renders the same seed on the **ungraded** model, and the image node grades that render afterwards. Set the same wheels on both grade nodes to see how differently a grade lands when the model composes in it and when it is laid over a finished picture.\n\n`strength` scales the whole grade; `start_percent` / `end_percent` limit it to part of the schedule."
   ],
   "color": "#432",
   "bgcolor": "#653"
  },
